From 8ccf82f6f7a591284b274eae20e4f2b84bf1f867 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 07:14:47 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fixup! logging: write log lines on a logger thread

Separate the 512-record wake threshold from burst capacity and reserve 131072 lazy slots per thread. With the JSON test sidecar, compactblocks still dropped 44787 lines at16384 slots and4482 at65536; the131072 candidate passes that reproducer and bounded IBD/relay. The ring reserves64MiB plus704B metadata while a local startup allocation control touched32KiB. Full-suite validation remains a separate gate; no user sizing or blocking-mode flag is introduced.
---
 doc/logging-async.md | 26 +++++++++++++++++++++-----
 src/logging.cpp      |  4 ++--
 src/logging.h        | 10 ++++++----
 3 files changed, 29 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/doc/logging-async.md b/doc/logging-async.md
index 4e23a86f25..9865148a85 100644
--- a/doc/logging-async.md
+++ b/doc/logging-async.md
@@ -31,8 +31,24 @@ record itself. Explicit Flush, or a deliberately paused/stopped worker, may
 render on the calling thread. Tests changing options or callbacks must Flush
 first: those changes apply when records are written, not when queued.
 
-At the inherited capacity of 1,024 records, slot storage is 512 KiB per
-prepared thread, plus the reserved record and metadata. Slots are not zeroed
-at construction: reserved address space and resident memory are different.
-This capacity is not yet claimed sufficient for the realistic-load zero-drop
-requirement; ring sizing is a separate measured gate.
+The capacity is 131,072 records per prepared thread: 64 MiB of queue slots,
+plus one 512-byte severe overflow record and metadata (704 bytes total beyond
+slots on the tested macOS arm64 ABI). A ring reserves this address space;
+record object lifetimes begin only when slots are claimed, so unused slot
+pages are not initialized. A local allocation control measured a 32 KiB
+initial RSS increase for this 131,072-slot raw-storage candidate. Resident memory can grow to the full
+ring size under load. Thread-local pointers, allocation bookkeeping and the
+registry containers add their own overhead.
+
+The original typed-slot array default-constructed source_location in every
+record, touching every page even though its constructor did not clear the
+whole payload. The raw byte storage avoids that eager residency; each claimed
+slot is placement-constructed before publication and read after acquire.
+Records must remain trivially destructible; reference payloads are still
+released by the consumer before their slot is reused.
+
+Wake notifications retain the original 512-record threshold, independently of
+burst capacity. No user-facing sizing option is added. This is burst capacity,
+not a promise to buffer an indefinitely stalled sink. Sustained artificial
+floods may still drop; measurements must report accepted, dropped and actually
+written counts.
diff --git a/src/logging.cpp b/src/logging.cpp
index 1ffb41234b..5cbde91b40 100644
--- a/src/logging.cpp
+++ b/src/logging.cpp
@@ -874,8 +874,8 @@ void BCLog::Logger::Enqueue(std::string_view str, std::string *owned,
     }
     if (ring->Commit() && !m_wake_requested.load(std::memory_order_relaxed) &&
         !m_wake_requested.exchange(true)) {
-        // The ring is half full: wake the logger thread now rather than at
-        // its next tick (one notification per wake-up, rare).
+        // The ring reached its wake threshold: wake the logger now rather than
+        // at its next tick (one notification per wake-up, rare).
         m_wake = true;
         m_wake_cv.notify_one();
     }
diff --git a/src/logging.h b/src/logging.h
index 22a4af26fb..462794fc8e 100644
--- a/src/logging.h
+++ b/src/logging.h
@@ -294,7 +294,9 @@ class LogRing {
     LogRecord m_emergency;
 
 public:
-    static constexpr size_t CAPACITY{1024};
+    static constexpr size_t CAPACITY{131072};
+    static constexpr size_t WAKE_THRESHOLD{512};
+    static_assert(WAKE_THRESHOLD <= CAPACITY);
     static_assert((CAPACITY & (CAPACITY - 1)) == 0);
 
     //! User-provided, so unused slot bytes are not initialized: their pages
@@ -317,17 +319,17 @@ public:
     }
     /**
      * Producer: publish the slot returned by Claim. Returns true while the
-     * ring is at least half full (time to wake the logger thread).
+     * ring has reached the wake threshold (independent of burst capacity).
      */
     bool Commit() noexcept {
         const uint64_t head{m_head.load(std::memory_order_relaxed) + 1};
         m_head.store(head, std::memory_order_release);
-        if (head - m_cached_tail < CAPACITY / 2) {
+        if (head - m_cached_tail < WAKE_THRESHOLD) {
             return false;
         }
         // Possibly: look at the consumer's progress (only while backed up).
         m_cached_tail = m_tail.load(std::memory_order_acquire);
-        return head - m_cached_tail >= CAPACITY / 2;
+        return head - m_cached_tail >= WAKE_THRESHOLD;
     }
     /** Producer: count a line dropped because the ring was full */
     void CountDrop() noexcept {
-- 
